v0.2.0 - Enterprise Planning Engine

Status: Phase 1 implemented, pending review

Phase 1 - Architecture, Database, API

Architecture decisions

- Added a dedicated backend Planning module to keep enterprise planning contracts separate from the existing task CRUD surface.
- Reused existing task hierarchy, task dependency, and project baseline concepts where they are already stable.
- Kept scheduling calculations out of the frontend and behind PlanningService. Phase 1 stores pending schedule snapshots; Phase 2 will replace those with calculated schedule/task rows.
- Added resource planning as first-class backend data: capacity, allocation, and workload heat-map snapshots.
- Added portfolio dependency data separately from single-project task dependencies so executive timeline and roadmap APIs can support cross-project planning.
- Preserved existing schema and endpoints. All Phase 1 tables are additive.

